  "body": "This is in respect to section 8.11. I have been implementing this in WebKit[1] and some questions have come up as to whether it's expected that animation frames between the main thread and a worker should be synchronised.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I think that there can't be an expectation of synchronisation, given that the main thread can be interrupted out-of-band with a worker thread, but does that carry over into it being ok that animation frames may be provided at different rates even when the main thread isn't interrupted?\r\n\r\nI think a clarifying paragraph or sentence wouldn't be unreasonable. Something along the lines of \"Animation frames delivered in workers may not be delivered at the same rate as those on the main thread.\"\r\n\r\n[1] https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=202525",
